content.text:
Chapter 2 is corrected. The build, the commands that compile the library, and the section about the caches are gone.

The page: https://palimondo.github.io/fortress/specification/revival/overview.html

One sentence replaces them: "The commands of this chapter assume an installed implementation, with the command `fortress` on the shell's path; the file `README.md` of the repository says how to build one."

Sections 2.1 to 2.3 now contain only these subjects:

- how to write a program;
- how to run it with the interpreter: `fortress HelloWorld.fss`;
- how to compile it and run it: `fortress compile HelloWorld.fss`, then `fortress run HelloWorld`;
- a program in two files with an api: `fortress link Blargh.fss`, then `fortress run Blargh`;
- how to generate an api from a component: `fortress api Zeepf.fss`.

The worker ran each command again, and each output agrees with the text. I read the new section 2.1 on the built page. No page of the Working Draft changed, so your notes stay in their positions.

The names `Zeepf` and `Blargh` are still there. They wait for your answer: 1, plain names (`Messages` and `Main`); 2, the names of the team stay.

